    <!-- 1. Data Handling & Student Privacy -->
    <section style="margin-bottom:40px">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.45rem; font-weight:800; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:12px; border-bottom:2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom:8px">1. Data Handling &amp; Privacy by Design</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.7; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:14px">
        ClipSAT is architected with a <strong>privacy-first posture</strong> designed to comply with the Saudi Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) and international privacy best practices:
      </p>
      <ul style="padding-left:20px; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:16px">
        <li><strong>Local Storage by Default:</strong> By default, all study activity — streak counts, chapter completions, practice test scores, flashcard schedules, and mistake logs — is saved solely in your device's browser local storage. It remains on your device until you decide to create a cloud account or clear your cache.</li>
        <li><strong>Optional Cloud Accounts:</strong> When you register for an optional account or ClipSAT Plus, your data is securely stored using Supabase infrastructure. Access is isolated via PostgreSQL Row Level Security (RLS) policies, ensuring only your authenticated session can access your study history.</li>
        <li><strong>IP Logging &amp; Infrastructure Security:</strong> Like all cloud applications, backend infrastructure providers (Supabase and Cloudflare) temporarily log client IP addresses strictly for rate limiting, DDoS defense, and security audit logs. These operational logs are retained for standard operational windows (typically up to 30 days) and are never used to track browsing history across other websites.</li>
        <li><strong>No Data Brokering:</strong> ClipSAT never sells, rents, or monetizes student data. We do not run third-party tracker networks or behavioral data brokers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="font-size:.92rem; color:var(--muted)">
        For full legal specifications, review our complete <a href="/privacy/" style="color:var(--indigo); text-decoration:underline">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/cookies/" style="color:var(--indigo); text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Academic Rigor & Content Quality -->
    <section style="margin-bottom:40px">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.45rem; font-weight:800; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:12px; border-bottom:2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom:8px">2. Curriculum Alignment &amp; Mathematical Rigor</h2>
      <p style="line-height:1.7; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:14px">
        Every question, proof, and lesson on ClipSAT is authored with academic precision:
      </p>
      <ul style="padding-left:20px; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:16px">
        <li><strong>Curriculum-Authentic:</strong> Content matches the actual testing formats of Cambridge International (0580 / 9709), College Board (AP &amp; Digital SAT), ACT, IB Math (AA/AI), and Qiyas (GAT Qudrat &amp; SAAT Tahsili).</li>
        <li><strong>Step-by-Step Proofs &amp; Socratic Hints:</strong> We do not provide only letter answers. Practice problems and worked examples include detailed derivation steps so learners understand the underlying theorems.</li>
        <li><strong>Real Scale &amp; Formula Consistency:</strong> Diagrams and canvas visualizers are geometrically accurate and plotted to mathematical scale.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. AI Disclosure & Pedagogical Boundaries -->
    <section style="margin-bottom:40px">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.45rem; font-weight:800; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:12px; border-bottom:2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom:8px">3. AI Disclosure &amp; Pedagogical Guardrails</h2>
      <div style="background:var(--panel, #fff); border:1.5px solid var(--line); border-left:4px solid var(--amber, #d97706); border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:16px">
        <strong style="color:var(--text); font-size:.98rem; display:block; margin-bottom:6px">Transparency Notice: AI-Powered Learning Assistant</strong>
        <p style="margin:0; font-size:.92rem; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.6">
          The interactive chat tool on ClipSAT is named the <strong>ClipSAT AI Tutor</strong>. It is powered by artificial intelligence language models (routed securely via private proxy), not human tutors. While highly capable, AI models can produce mathematical or step errors. Output is not a substitute for teacher instruction, and students should verify critical calculations.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul style="padding-left:20px; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:16px">
        <li><strong>Strict Mathematics Guardrail:</strong> The ClipSAT AI Tutor is strictly restricted to mathematics and quantitative exam preparation. It automatically declines non-academic topics, ensuring student focus and safety.</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy of Prompts:</strong> Student questions submitted to the AI tutor route through secure server proxies. Prompts are never used to train public foundation models without consent.</li>
        <li><strong>AI-Assisted Question Bank Review:</strong> Where question variations are generated with AI assistance, they pass automated rule verification and educator review before inclusion in practice pools.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

